<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:38:00 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>French PM Lecornu says aid available 'immediately' to rebuild fire-hit regions</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-french-pm-lecornu-says-aid-available-immediately-to-rebuild-fire-hit-regions</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu on Monday announced aid worth €12 million to help residents of the southwest hit by wildfires rebuild their lives. He was heckled earlier in the day by dozens of locals in the town of Le Porge in the Gironde region, who said they were unhappy with the government's response.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b92d9c8-9a5e-11f1-aa90-15d3b6b8ca68</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:23:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fe13c2a8-8dd4-11f1-a326-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NU.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Iran bars two French diplomats over alleged 'interference'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-iran-bars-two-french-diplomats-over-alleged-interference</link><description>
Iran has said ​that two French embassy employees who were briefly detained last month following a ​diplomatic dispute will not be allowed to return to Iran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7580d2a-9a2a-11f1-97ca-c954d7c983a2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:33:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3a30ab80-89b0-11f1-afab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96TM9DK.jpg">© AFP - Atta Kenare</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Cop17 aims to restore land and hope in fight against desertification</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260817-cop17-aims-to-restore-land-and-hope-in-fight-against-desertification</link><description>
Extreme weather across much of Europe and elsewhere is lending added weight to the United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification (Cop17), which begins on Monday in Mongolia. RFI looks at what's at stake worldwide. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/614acb7c-3108-11ef-b594-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_33V82Y9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/614acb7c-3108-11ef-b594-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_33V82Y9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5c1b8fec-9a1f-11f1-820b-111cad60ec80</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:52:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/614acb7c-3108-11ef-b594-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_33V82Y9.jpg">© Karel Prinsloo / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Migrants stranded in Ceuta say ‘I’d rather die here than go back to Morocco’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260817-migrants-stranded-in-ceuta-say-i-d-rather-die-here-than-go-back-to-morocco</link><description>
Nearly three weeks after a mass border crossing brought tens of thousands of migrants into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta, thousands remain stranded in precarious conditions, Maria Jimenez, spokesperson for the NGO Elin, told RFI. She said many still lack adequate shelter, food and medical care.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3eca97cc-9a19-11f1-8e9f-33840bc1377b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:48:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg">AP Photo/STR - STR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Devastated by wildfire, the village of Le Porge pins hopes for support on PM visit</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260817-devastated-by-wildfire-the-village-of-le-porge-pins-hopes-for-support-on-pm-visit</link><description>
Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu will visit the Gironde department in southwestern France on Monday to launch reconstruction efforts, after the area fell victim to the most destructive wildfires seen in 70 years. The mayor of Le Porge – one of the villages worst affected – told RFI he's hoping for government support to rebuild its economy, which relies heavily on forest exploitation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">006ea6ee-9636-11f1-af94-35fc75775395</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 05:13:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69b874be-9662-11f1-82a8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/260810-Le-Porge-burnt-traffic-sign3.jpg">© RFI/Jan van der Made</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Cameroon beat Malawi to claim maiden Women’s Cup of Nations title</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260817-cameroon-beat-malawi-to-claim-maiden-women-s-cup-of-nations-title-wafcon</link><description>
Cameroon claimed a first Women’s Africa Cup of Nations (WAFCON) title when they beat Malawi 3-0 in Sunday's final in Morocco, with Marie Ngah Manga’s first-half double helping the the Indomitable Lionesses seal victory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7acc54b8-9a0f-11f1-a80e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26228796067115.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7acc54b8-9a0f-11f1-a80e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26228796067115.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f302cc7e-99ff-11f1-8047-1bb489ce5498</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 06:40:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7acc54b8-9a0f-11f1-a80e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26228796067115.jpg">AP Photo/</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ex-PM Attal urges Macron to put under-15 social media ban to referendum</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260816-ex-pm-attal-urges-macron-to-put-under-15-social-media-ban-to-referendum</link><description>
Gabriel Attal has called on President Emmanuel Macron to put a proposed ban on social media for children under 15 directly to French voters, after the Constitutional Council struck down legislation approved by parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6f3b6e46-9955-11f1-adb7-9f8fc4277402</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:30:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8acb7a0-1e30-11f1-8f66-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24066822349898.jpg">AP - Jenny Kane</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Belgium turns to European air support as wildfire rages near German border</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-belgium-turns-to-european-air-support-as-wildfire-rages-near-german-border</link><description>
Belgium called in aerial reinforcements from across Europe on Sunday as firefighters battled the country’s largest wildfire in more than a century, with flames spreading rapidly through a difficult-to-reach nature reserve near the German border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdccd256-9955-11f1-9ad6-2b9ea6a90619</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:24:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Europe's shrinking rivers give rise to debate over how to tackle drought</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260816-europe-s-shrinking-rivers-give-rise-to-debate-over-how-to-tackle-drought</link><description>
Europe's shrinking rivers are disrupting industry, reducing power generation and intensifying the debate over how to respond to worsening drought. As water levels fall across the continent, authorities and businesses alike are looking for ways to keep freight moving and critical infrastructure operating. Hydrologists warn, however, that digging rivers deeper cannot create more water and could make shortages worse.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b280094-97ca-11f1-90af-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:17:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/501dd132-9056-11f1-aee0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26209461327444.jpg">© Federico Gambarini/DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Solar-powered community gardens offer lifeline in drought-hit Zimbabwe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260816-solar-powered-community-gardens-offer-lifeline-in-drought-hit-zimbabwe</link><description>
At a shared garden in eastern Zimbabwe, solar-powered pumps are helping farmers grow crops year round, even when drought dries out other fields. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9d4442e-97c7-11f1-a081-371e64013e18</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:53:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81a7bf68-97c4-11f1-a9f5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Berita-Numbi-in-Mutekwatekwa-community-garden-in-Mutare-RFI-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpg">© Farai Shawn Matiashe</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Obesity rises sharply as French Polynesia faces chronic health challenges</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260816-obesity-rises-sharply-as-french-polynesia-faces-chronic-health-challenges</link><description>
French Polynesia is facing growing public health pressures as rising rates of chronic disease combine with an ageing population and changing lifestyles. More than half of adult residents are now considered obese.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">142ad854-9570-11f1-80d1-6bca3bd6865c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:31:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6609f082-9571-11f1-8997-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/French-Polynesia-Obesity.jpg">© AFP - THEO ROUBY </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Morocco arrests nearly 300 migrants near Ceuta amid renewed crossing fears</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-morocco-arrests-nearly-300-migrants-near-ceuta-amid-renewed-crossing-fears</link><description>
Scores of would-be migrants, most of them from sub-Saharan Africa, were intercepted in northern Morocco near the border with the Spanish exclave of Ceuta on Saturday, two weeks after tens of thousands of people attempted to enter the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">796023ce-9957-11f1-bc95-7f396f569dcf</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:13:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg">AP Photo/Bernat Armangue - Bernat Armangue</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France probes unprecedented cyberattack after tax data of 678,000 users stolen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-probes-unprecedented-cyberattack-after-tax-data-of-678-000-users-stolen</link><description>
French prosecutors have opened an investigation into a major cyberattack on the country’s tax administration that affected nearly 700,000 individuals and businesses, authorities said on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ef8055a-98b7-11f1-8465-5f55dfe1c00c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:50:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f31b1d0-98b7-11f1-ac38-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cyber-attack.jpg">© Freepix</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's successive heatwaves show strain of living in urban 'heat islands'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260815-france-s-successive-heatwaves-highlight-strain-of-living-in-urban-heat-islands</link><description>
As France experiences its latest heatwave, residents of urban "heat islands" – dense neighbourhoods with few trees or green spaces – are suffering acutely in the high temperatures, and local authorities are searching for solutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e08ea958-97db-11f1-ac97-c132d391fb73</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:43:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a0ac01ac-5275-11f0-b313-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/36a61f85-934d-4cd7-acd5-e4137a8ee89a.jpeg">© Théo Renaudon/RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Algeria edge Morocco on penalties in WAFCON third-place play-off</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260816-algeria-edge-morocco-on-penalties-in-wafcon-third-place-play-off</link><description>
Morocco endured a second painful penalty shootout defeat in the space of four days as Algeria claimed third place at the Women’s Africa Cup of Nations on Saturday following a 1-1 draw in Rabat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f95da7bc-98b8-11f1-aa82-e12dd09773c0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:26:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8de40ee-98e9-11f1-899e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-08-15-at-22-41-10-L-Alg%C3%A9rie-s-offre-le-bronze-au-bout-du-suspense-face-au-Maroc.png">© Courtesy of CAF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Armenian Genocide survivors' grandson says 'political motives' block recognition</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-armenian-survivor-s-grandson-says-politics-still-blocks-genocide-recognition</link><description>
In 1915, the Ottoman Empire began the systematic deportation and massacre of its Armenian population. As many as 1.5 million Armenians were killed – widely regarded by historians as the twentieth century's first genocide, and the event for which the term was later coined. Stephan Pechdimaldji, the grandson of two of the survivors, spoke to RFI about why recognition still matters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">221a786c-969b-11f1-83af-a5d44a90634e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:03:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - MARIO TAMA</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Five years into Taliban rule, Afghanistan seeks to ease international isolation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-five-years-into-taliban-rule-afghanistan-seeks-to-ease-international-isolation</link><description>
In the five years since the Taliban seized back power in Afghanistan, the country's worsening human rights record has drawn sanctions and aid cuts. But despite refusing to officially recognise the fundamentalist movement's government, some countries are concluding that engaging with the Taliban has become unavoidable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d87aa374-96f1-11f1-938b-1bb6596caa4b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 07:21:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg">© AP - Hedayat Shah </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Law on assisted dying wins constitutional approval in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-law-on-assisted-dying-wins-constitutional-approval-in-france</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council on Friday approved a law creating a right to assisted dying, removing the last major legal obstacle before the measure can be enacted and implemented.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26163be6-97ee-11f1-94eb-8707596c334a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:11:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e3cd768-77a2-11ed-a3cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_15M4NW.jpg">© AFP - JEAN-CHRISTOPHE VERHAEGEN </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Top French court scraps social media ban for children under 15</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260814-top-french-court-scraps-social-media-ban-for-children-under-15</link><description>
France's Constitutional Council struck down a law on Friday that would have banned children under 15 from using social media from September. The judges ruled that the measure placed a disproportionate restriction on freedom of expression and communication.
